  Thank you for submitting your public records request to the Oregon Park=
s and Recreation Department (OPRD).  =C2=A0  Expect to hear back from us =
in about 10 business days with any records that match your request or, fo=
r larger requests, with an estimate for staff time and costs to gather th=
e documents.  =C2=A0  Thank you,  Oregon Parks and Recreation Department =
=C2=A0     =0D
                           =0D
                            On=0D
                            Thu, 2 Apr at  1:23 PM=0D
                            ,  Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>  wro=
te:=0D
                           =0D
                           =0D
                             =0D
OREGON PARKS AND RECREATION DEPARTMENT =0D
 =0D
Public Records Request =0D
 =0D
Pursuant to ORS 192.311 et seq. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
To Whom It May Concern, =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
I am submitting this public records request as a supplement to my previou=
s public records request submitted on August 22, 2025. I am requesting al=
l records generated from August 22, 2025 to present that were not produce=
d in response to that request, as well=0D
 as the following specific records related to a new incident. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
On March 24, 2026 =E2=80=94 the one-year anniversary of my dismissal from=
 Honeyman State Park =E2=80=94 three law enforcement officers arrived at =
my residence at the Siltcoos Work Center, U.S. Forest Service, located at=
 82900 Highway 101, Florence, Oregon 97439. One of those=0D
 officers was U.S. Forest Service Special Agent Matthew Oliver. The state=
d reason for the visit was concern about content I had posted online. Tha=
t content is the public archive at oprdvolunteerabuse.org, which document=
s my treatment as a volunteer at Honeyman=0D
 State Park and the subsequent institutional response. Oregon plate 731 Q=
RV was recorded on camera at the scene. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
I am requesting the following records: =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
All communications between any OPRD employee or official and U.S. Forest =
Service Special Agent Matthew Oliver or any other Forest Service employee=
, from January 1, 2025 to present. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
All communications between any OPRD employee or official and any Oregon S=
tate Police officer or official referencing my name, my volunteer service=
, or my online archive, from January 1, 2025 to present. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
All communications between any OPRD employee or official and any Lane Cou=
nty Sheriff's Office employee referencing my name, my volunteer service, =
or my online archive, from January 1, 2025 to present. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
All internal communications referencing my name (Robert Samuel White), my=
 online archive, or the domain oprdvolunteerabuse.org from August 22, 202=
5 to present. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
All records related to any coordination, consultation, or communication b=
etween OPRD and any law enforcement agency in connection with my online a=
rchive or public statements. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
Oregon public records law requires a response within five business days. =
My previous request was met with a 90-day silence that constituted a viol=
ation of ORS 192.324. I expect full compliance with the statutory timelin=
e. If any records are withheld, please=0D
 provide a written explanation citing the specific statutory exemption cl=
aimed for each withheld record. =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
 =0D
I am requesting a fee waiver on the grounds that this request serves the =
public interest and will contribute to public understanding of how a stat=
e agency coordinates with law enforcement in response to a citizen's prot=
ected speech. =0D
